Body:
**Update — confirmed fixed on my end.**  

@maurerle was right about the cost scale — my values were per-token instead of per-1M-tokens. That fixed the `$0.00` display.
However, I also had two **related config gaps** that left the UI broken even after fixing costs:
### 1. `limit.context` is required for the % usage display
OpenCode uses `model.limit.context` for the percentage calculation, **not** `model.context_window`. Without it, context always shows `0%` regardless of actual token usage.
### 2. `includeUsage: true` is needed in provider options
When using `@ai-sdk/openai-compatible` with a LiteLLM proxy, streaming responses don't include token counts by default. Both cost *and* context tracking fail silently without this flag.
### Full working config excerpt
```json
{
  "provider": {
    "litellm": {
      "npm": "@ai-sdk/openai-compatible",
      "options": {
        "baseURL": "https://proxy.example.com/v1",
        "includeUsage": true
      },
      "models": {
        "my-model": {
          "limit": { "context": 202000, "output": 25344 },
          "cost": { "input": 1.4, "output": 4.4 }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

All three (cost scale, limit.context, includeUsage) were required to get cost tracking and context percentage working correctly.

---
Closing this as resolved — the underlying behavior could use better docs, but it's working as designed once configured properly.
